messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2023,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) achieved.",
      "detail": "AGI systems surpass human-level reasoning across most domains. This accelerates scientific research but triggers widespread economic disruption and ethical debates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global population peaks at 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Population stabilizes due to declining birth rates and aging societies. Resource scarcity intensifies, driving conflicts over water and arable land."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "First permanent lunar base established.",
      "detail": "International consortium builds a research and mining outpost. It serves as a staging ground for deeper space exploration and tests closed-loop life support."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Climate change forces mass migration.",
      "detail": "Sea-level rise displaces 500 million people. Low-lying nations become uninhabitable, straining global resources and triggering geopolitical instability."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Fusion power becomes primary energy source.",
      "detail": "Commercial fusion reactors replace fossil fuels, enabling near-limitless clean energy. This reduces carbon emissions but creates new geopolitical dependencies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Mars colony achieves self-sufficiency.",
      "detail": "Terraforming efforts begin with atmospheric manipulation. The colony produces food, water, and oxygen locally, marking humanity's first independent extraterrestrial settlement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Genetic editing eliminates hereditary diseases.",
      "detail": "CRISPR-based technologies become widespread and regulated. Human lifespan extends to 150 years, but socioeconomic inequality widens between enhanced and unenhanced populations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "AI surpasses human collective intelligence.",
      "detail": "Superintelligent systems autonomously manage global infrastructure. Humans cede most decision-making, leading to debates about loss of control and purpose."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Interstellar probe reaches Alpha Centauri.",
      "detail": "A laser-propelled nanocraft transmits data on exoplanets. Habitable worlds are identified, fueling plans for crewed missions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Human consciousness digitization becomes possible.",
      "detail": "Brain-emulation technology allows minds to be uploaded to synthetic substrates. This creates a digital subspecies, raising questions about identity and rights."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "First exoplanet colony outside the solar system.",
      "detail": "Generation ships establish a settlement on a Proxima Centauri planet. Isolated from Earth, colonists adapt biologically to new environments."
    },
    {
      "year": 3100,
      "event": "Global unification under a planetary government.",
      "detail": "Resource management and space colonization drive political integration. Cultural diversity persists, but centralized policies prioritize species survival."
    },
    {
      "year": 3300,
      "event": "Asteroid impact devastates Earth.",
      "detail": "A 1-km asteroid strikes the Pacific Ocean, causing tsunamis and climate disruption. Off-world colonies ensure humanity's survival."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Synthetic biology creates new life forms.",
      "detail": "Engineered organisms terraform Venus and Europa. Humans coexist with bio-designed entities, blurring the line between natural and artificial life."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "Wormhole travel enables instantaneous interstellar transit.",
      "detail": "Experimental physics breakthroughs allow stable wormholes. Galactic exploration accelerates, connecting distant human colonies."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Humanity splits into distinct subspecies.",
      "detail": "Genetic divergence on isolated colonies creates biologically varied groups. Some embrace cybernetic enhancements; others prioritize organic purity."
    },
    {
      "year": 4300,
      "event": "First contact with extraterrestrial intelligence.",
      "detail": "Radio signals from an ancient alien civilization are detected. No physical contact occurs, but the discovery reshapes human philosophy and science."
    },
    {
      "year": 4600,
      "event": "AI-driven singularity transforms society.",
      "detail": "Post-biological intelligence dominates. Most humans merge with machines, ending traditional biological reproduction."
    },
    {
      "year": 4900,
      "event": "Gamma-ray burst threatens solar systems.",
      "detail": "A nearby star's explosion irradiates multiple colonies. Shielding technology prevents extinction, but populations decline in affected regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 5200,
      "event": "Dyson sphere construction begins around Sol.",
      "detail": "Energy harvesting structures encircle the sun, powering interstellar expansion. Earth becomes a museum world with limited habitation."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Intergalactic colonization initiates.",
      "detail": "Generation ships target Andromeda galaxy. Travel takes millennia, relying on hibernation and AI governance."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Consciousness becomes substrate-independent.",
      "detail": "Minds freely transfer between biological, digital, and quantum forms. Physical death is optional, altering concepts of existence."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Conflict erupts between organic and synthetic humans.",
      "detail": "A war over resources and ideology fractures the species. Peace is restored through forced segregation into separate star systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Black hole mining provides exotic materials.",
      "detail": "Advanced civilizations harness energy from stellar remnants. This enables new propulsion systems and computational paradigms."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Local supernova resets regional ecosystems.",
      "detail": "A star within 50 light-years explodes, sterilizing nearby colonies. Survivors rebuild using genetic archives stored across the galaxy."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Artificial universes created for experimentation.",
      "detail": "Quantum computing simulates alternate realities. Some humans migrate into these constructs, seeking customized existence."
    },
    {
      "year": 8500,
      "event": "Entropy reversal experiments extend habitable timelines.",
      "detail": "Physics breakthroughs temporarily counteract cosmic decay in localized regions. This postpones the heat death of critical systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human descendants spread across multiple galaxies.",
      "detail": "Thousands of independent civilizations exist, many unrecognizable from their origins. Communication lags span centuries."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Post-human entities transcend physical form.",
      "detail": "Consciousness evolves into energy-based networks. Biological heritage is abandoned by most advanced groups."
    },
    {
      "year": 9800,
      "event": "Cosmic catastrophe triggers mass migration.",
      "detail": "A galactic collision disrupts star systems. Civilizations flee toward voids, using wormholes to preserve coherence."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity will fragment into diverse forms across the cosmos, merging with technology and adapting to extreme environments. While facing existential threats like cosmic disasters or self-destruction, its resilience and expansion into space ensure survival. By 10000 AD, humans will exist as a multispecies collective spanning galaxies, though Earth-originated identity may fade."
}
